    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP today, we are leaning heavily into the top-of-the-order firepower and favorable park factors to anchor our daily projections. **Mickey Moniak** leads the charge with a 75.98 efficiency score, benefiting from a prime matchup against Lugo in a high-scoring park environment, bolstered by a substantial +14% platoon advantage. Right on his heels, **James Wood** (75.37) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.71) are locked in as essential starts; **James Wood** boasts elite xwOBA metrics and a favorable matchup against Ritchie, while **Tyler Soderstrom** thrives with a significant +10% park boost and the benefit of hitting second against Montero. **Brice Turang** rounds out our high-efficiency tier at 72.38, maximizing his value with a +10% boost for occupying the leadoff spot against Ure\u00f1a.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Austin Riley**, who yielded a score of 46.04. While his power upside is usually undeniable, the optimizer relegated him to the bench due to a difficult matchup against Cavalli\u2014an elite arm with a 3.48 xERA\u2014combined with a suppressed batting order position. Conversely, we are keeping **Corbin Carroll** active despite a marginal 58.33 score; even with a tough matchup against Williams, his elite speed is too critical to sacrifice in our quest for stolen bases, especially when weighted against the risk of leaving scarce production on the wire. We are exercising caution with **Jose Caballero**, whose 55.06 score is dragged down by a -5% wind-in penalty and a tough matchup against a team with an elite holding strategy for stolen bases. Keep a close eye on **Dalton Rushing** and **Zach McKinstry**; both are hovering near our 40-point floor and rely on their secondary skills to remain viable starters today.",
